From 163c6673221f7a79760659e65c560721ab1480a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:28:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freebsd: devices at another path become links into the
 container's devfs

A block volume reaches the container as a CRI device: the kubelet's link
to the disk (an md(4), da(4), ... in devfs) at the pod's devicePath, such
as /mnt/volume1. devfs can't show a device under another name, so unhide
it at its own name and make devicePath, in the container's root file
system, a symbolic link to it. Host path volumes of a device at another
path get the same. A path below /dev stays an error (the devfs would hide
the link), and so do configured devices (additional_devices).

The kubelet's host path is a link: resolve it before looking for devfs.
---
 internal/config/device/device_freebsd.go     |  3 +
 internal/devfs/devfs_freebsd.go              | 62 ++++++++++++++++++--
 internal/devfs/devfs_freebsd_test.go         | 36 +++++++++++-
